<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes market participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes market participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 1.816 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    342 days   22.28 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   21.76 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   20.81 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     31 days   19.10 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     17 days   18.99 pct</p>
<p>    166 million	3 days   17.94 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
